WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.611
The KL Divergence

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:02.637
Is Never Negative

00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:03.887
Except in PyTorch

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:05.577
An exploration of

00:00:05.389 --> 00:00:06.804
why KL divergence

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:07.452
can come out

00:00:07.264 --> 00:00:08.620
negative in PyTorch

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:10.282
despite the mathematics

00:00:10.094 --> 00:00:11.002
saying it never

00:00:10.814 --> 00:00:11.356
should

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.352
Among scalar families

00:00:13.163 --> 00:00:14.472
in ordinary parameter

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:14.967
ranges

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.724
over 85% of

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:18.340
FP32 values have

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:19.307
at least 1%

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.191
relative error near

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:20.970
KL 10

00:00:21.064 --> 00:00:22.113
FP16

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:22.903
10

00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:24.484
and about 30%

00:00:24.295 --> 00:00:25.533
become negative at

00:00:25.345 --> 00:00:26.760
smaller divergences

00:00:27.278 --> 00:00:28.492
More precision is

00:00:28.304 --> 00:00:29.176
not the cure

00:00:29.353 --> 00:00:30.815
evaluated one precision

00:00:30.627 --> 00:00:31.263
higher

00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:32.619
the same formulas

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:34.766
still leave 7--51%

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.476
of FP32 values

00:00:36.441 --> 00:00:37.714
significantly wrong

00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:38.940
for 22 of

00:00:38.752 --> 00:00:40.438
23 configurations

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:41.988
Full story on

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:42.695
the dashboard
